{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/988622-setting-idea-the-sterile-chronicle","id":988622,"title":"Setting Idea: The Sterile Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-16T19:49:46-07:00","id":988622,"title":"Setting Idea: The Sterile Chronicle","content":"It's the year 2205, and the world is at peace. Life is good, Tech is state of the art, Entertainment is all-engrossing, and the average person lives to the age of 105. All is good, except for one issue. The youngest person is now 5 years old, and he was born December 31st, 2199. It has been 5 years since there has been a birth. For some reason, Humanity as a whole has gone completely sterile, and if a solution isn't found soon, this could very well be an end to Humanity's existence. We are entering the Sterile Era. May God help us. Please, free us from this curse.<br /> <br /> A planned, full Crossover-Chronicle with all 11 Major Monster Types, spanning 150+ years, from the birth of the last child, to the breath of the last man. See how both Mortal and Monster live in the last era of humanity, and beyond, in the Monster Age.<br /> <br /> I plan to begin this once all CoD books are available for 2e, and when the Crossover Chronicle is available. What are your opinions of this story, and how would you think all the different types of Monsters would react to the slow death of Humanity, and afterwards, when all humans are gone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:55:46-07:00","id":988628,"title":"","content":"I hate to say this, but I can't imagine the human race 200 years from now can't clone some babies up.<br /> <br /> ...that said, a chronicle where the only source of new humans are Prometheans achieving the New Dawn might be an absolute blast. Or maybe none where no humans remain, and you have to rebuild what it means to be human?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:07:28-07:00","id":988640,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the God-Machine could will it so the clones end up as misshapened monsters 90% of the time. This is based on the mathematical Doomsday Argument, actually. It's why the date is 2200.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doomsday_argument#Analogy_to_the_estimated_final_score_of_a_cricket_batsman\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Population_curve.svg/1280px-Population_curve.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doomsday_argument#Analogy_to_the_estimated_final_score_of_a_cricket_batsman\" target=\"_blank\"> Doomsday argument - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doomsday_argument#Analogy_to_the_estimated_final_score_of_a_cricket_batsman\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doomsday_argument#Analogy_to_the_estimated_final_score_of_a_cricket_batsman </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:22:47-07:00","id":988651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/988622-setting-idea-the-sterile-chronicle?p=988628#post988628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate to say this, but I can't imagine the human race 200 years from now can't clone some babies up.<br /> <br /> ...that said, a chronicle where the only source of new humans are Prometheans achieving the New Dawn might be an absolute blast. Or maybe none where no humans remain, and you have to rebuild what it means to be human?</div> </div> </div> </div> I had a chronicle idea similar to this called &quot;humanity reversed&quot; where a group of prometheans, changelings, and infinite macabre aliens are competing to create &quot;the perfect human&quot; so they create an offspring that doesn't immediately want to destroy them (changelings are based on the alien fae idea from changeling, so they don't trust the aliens, and they also happen to hate the prometheans too).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T22:26:06-07:00","id":988698,"title":"","content":"So, Children of Men, but with supernaturals.<br /> <br /> I can dig it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T03:00:01-07:00","id":988755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/988622-setting-idea-the-sterile-chronicle?p=988628#post988628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate to say this, but I can't imagine the human race 200 years from now can't clone some babies up.</div> </div> </div> </div>If everyone is totally sterile they might not be able to get the necessary raw materials.<br /> <br /> Also, werewolves kind of make new werewolves the same way humans make more humans. What happens to them?<br /> <br /> Because if they can still reproduce then humanity will eventually just become 100% wolf blooded and everyone will have a Tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-17-2016, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T04:01:59-07:00","id":988776,"title":"","content":"From what I could tell, humans must reproduce with humans. Since humans are 100% sterile, werewolves can't reproduce. They can try to reproduce with each other, but the result of that is usually very bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T04:59:14-07:00","id":988791,"title":"","content":"Not in second edition. They can breed with each other just fine now. <br /> <br /> 'Course, if <i>only </i>werewolf-werewolf pairings are viable that's still a definite bottleneck. Wolf-blooded humans would be rare and therefore so would Awakenings from them. And I suspect new Embraces would be <i>heavily</i> discouraged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T05:05:44-07:00","id":988794,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure once I get the new books, a lot of my questions will be answered. But in general, would the extinction of humanity be bad for the supernaturals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T05:33:29-07:00","id":988804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/988622-setting-idea-the-sterile-chronicle?p=988794#post988794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure once I get the new books, a lot of my questions will be answered. But in general, would the extinction of humanity be bad for the supernaturals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only supernatural that would get any benefit from it would probably be demons since there's a good chance a timeline where all humanity became sterile would become abandoned by the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T05:37:20-07:00","id":988805,"title":"","content":"In general, there would be a few issues for supernaturals if humanity went extinct.<br /> <br /> Humans make up the bulk of vampires' food supply, either directly or indirectly, in the case of elders. The youngest can feed on animals (well, technically they <i>all</i> can, but the older ones find it very difficult) but since humans are also the source of said youngest then as time passes less and less vampires will be able to do that without spending willpower.<br /> <br /> I can really see two solutions here: A lot of ghouling to preserve as many humans as possible, and a lot of voluntary torpor to keep a decent fraction of vampires able to feed on them, or even more voluntary torpor to keep themselves able to feed on animals easily.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are going to be wholly reliant on themselves to bolster numbers, but they should be ok.<br /> <br /> Mages are former humans, and so will likely stem mostly from Werewolf or former Promethean stock<br /> <br /> Changelings likewise. But the Gentry might just find some new toys to play with.<br /> <br /> Sin Eaters are in the same boat as mages<br /> <br /> Demons are going to be more obvious to the God Machine. That's bad for them.<br /> <br /> Prometheans will be fine, albeit somewhat aimless. They might feel a duty to pursue the New Dawn with even more gusto than before.<br /> <br /> Beasts are in the same boat as Vampires, but with even less means to get around it. They'd probably hang around with them and feed off Ghouls. <br /> <br /> Mummys have lost their cult, which means their revival is going to be impaired, possibly limited to Sothic Turns.<br /> <br /> Hunters are boned, obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 10-17-2016, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T06:16:23-07:00","id":988822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/988622-setting-idea-the-sterile-chronicle?p=988805#post988805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, there would be a few issues for supernaturals if humanity went extinct.<br /> <br /> Humans make up the bulk of vampires' food supply, either directly or indirectly, in the case of elders. The youngest can feed on animals (well, technically they <i>all</i> can, but the older ones find it very difficult) but since humans are also the source of said youngest then as time passes less and less vampires will be able to do that without spending willpower.<br /> <br /> I can really see two solutions here: A lot of ghouling to preserve as many humans as possible, and a lot of voluntary torpor to keep a decent fraction of vampires able to feed on them, or even more voluntary torpor to keep themselves able to feed on animals easily.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are going to be wholly reliant on themselves to bolster numbers, but they should be ok.<br /> <br /> Mages are former humans, and so will likely stem mostly from Werewolf or former Promethean stock<br /> <br /> Changelings likewise. But the Gentry might just find some new toys to play with.<br /> <br /> Sin Eaters are in the same boat as mages<br /> <br /> Demons are going to be more obvious to the God Machine. That's bad for them.<br /> <br /> Prometheans will be fine, albeit somewhat aimless. They might feel a duty to pursue the New Dawn with even more gusto than before.<br /> <br /> Beasts are in the same boat as Vampires, but with even less means to get around it. They'd probably hang around with them and feed off Ghouls. <br /> <br /> Mummys have lost their cult, which means their revival is going to be impaired, possibly limited to Sothic Turns.<br /> <br /> Hunters are boned, obviously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for this, it'll be cool to see how this changes with the 2nd ed of the other books, along with how the Deviants would handle this situation, when they are eventually released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T06:23:53-07:00","id":988824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/988622-setting-idea-the-sterile-chronicle?p=988822#post988822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for this, it'll be cool to see how this changes with the 2nd ed of the other books, along with how the Deviants would handle this situation, when they are eventually released.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine remade would be created now and then during experiments to create new humans","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T06:25:43-07:00","id":988825,"title":"","content":"I would assume by the text, the youngest person recorded being 5 and all, that Werewolves can't reproduce either, with each other or otherwise; and given the theme I would encourage that notion to add the feeling of desperation to all sides; but that's just my opinion. I'm also assuming, by the same token, that Mages can't force fertility into being or conjure up people magically either for some unclear reason; probably the same with Geniuses if you run with those around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T06:32:00-07:00","id":988827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/988622-setting-idea-the-sterile-chronicle?p=988825#post988825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would assume by the text, the youngest person recorded being 5 and all, that Werewolves can't reproduce either, with each other or otherwise; and given the theme I would encourage that notion to add the feeling of desperation to all sides; but that's just my opinion. I'm also assuming, by the same token, that Mages can't force fertility into being or conjure up people magically either for some unclear reason; probably the same with Geniuses if you run with those around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that sounds good. I could make it so that all living things are no longer reproducing, and fertile-based Magic is also failing for some reason. I'm planning that the God-Machine is causing this supernatural sterility, and has been slowly turning the fertility dial down since the 1940s, when the atomic bombs fell. Once all life has died off, it would create new life on the barren planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T06:33:43-07:00","id":988829,"title":"","content":"Oh, well in that case everyone's going to starve pretty quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T06:36:27-07:00","id":988831,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* It's something I'll have to think of. I just got the idea off of the Doomsday Argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T09:05:28-07:00","id":988887,"title":"","content":"There is also the spirit side of things to consider as less humans would see a big change in the spiritual ecosystem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T11:08:41-07:00","id":988936,"title":"","content":"Well, Mages can pretty much make people whole cloth, the only thing they really lack is the ability to create souls. So I could see a program being instated to collect the souls of all humans right before the moment of death and soul jar it for later use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 10-17-2016, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T11:57:50-07:00","id":988961,"title":"","content":"These are really cool workarounds for a world where humanity is slowly dying. I don't have the books, so I didn't know that half of this stuff was possible. Still, a Mage is just one person, and I doubt he can save everyone. Things are hardly ever ideal, so this catastrophe would still be massive, since there are so few supernaturals compared to humans. (1-100, at the most? May make it 1-1000)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T15:39:49-07:00","id":989044,"title":"","content":"A single mage, sure, but there's an entire society of them. This isn't even including the big name players like archmages (or high level spirits) who probably <i>could</i> manage to do all of this solo.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this will be easy or an instant fix, mind you, just that the supernatural populations could deal with it if they were forced to have to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 10-17-2016, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T15:43:12-07:00","id":989045,"title":"","content":"To be fair the Archmages could just shunt reality onto a timeline where everything is fine, so perhaps it's best if we just ignore them here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T15:45:41-07:00","id":989046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/988622-setting-idea-the-sterile-chronicle?p=989045#post989045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair the Archmages could just shunt reality onto a timeline where everything is fine, so perhaps it's best if we just ignore them here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly was for the most part. I'm going into this assuming that all of the easiest fixes like just using enough power to say 'No, that isn't what's happening' isn't working for some reason. I'm mostly talking about huge area non-Imperial magic effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T15:48:50-07:00","id":989049,"title":"","content":"What you have to think is first the effect you want in your game, and second the time frame you want for this.<br /> <br /> Most of what was said is about how the supernaturals will fare at the last stages of humanity. Now to the game, proper:<br /> <br /> At the moment the youngest humans are 5 years old, its certain that <u>everyone, absolutely everyone</u> will see the danger and think of means to counteract this. Actualy, at this stage we have a fairly numerous and stable society, but already in total red allert. Each splat, and humanity proper, are going to search for a solution.<br /> <br /> Here is your major decision, if there <u>is</u> a solution. Its your call entirely. Maybe there is one that humanity can find for itself. Maybe one or more splats have the secret to recover the world. Maybe there is an answer, but it is more complex than what a single splat can achieve by itself. And maybe humanity is simply doomed, so to speak.<br /> <br /> The first decade or two is going to be relatively stable, but concerned. In one way or another, every splat so far are likely to worry about humanity's destiny. Most will put more strain on rules about not killing humans, but such humanitarian deeds are going to be eventualy compensed by the horror of human experimentation, as the less humane of monsters try to find an answer.<br /> <br /> Passing this, humanity start to dwindle slowly. That will probably bring the fall of the Secret, as supernaturals become more numerous in proportion, even if some of they somehow try to keep their own numbers in check (probable for vampires). It means both less ways to hide and less reason to do so. Chaos will probably start here at some point, at least in human society.<br /> <br /> In the last decades, if no way out is found, are the moments of final decline. Without humanity, supernatural societies are likely to decline themselves, in a similar but delayed manner. It is probable that abundant chaos from the previous period start to revert as there is less to do. There is nothing to do about the coming end, and everyone alive is old and tired. The world does have much more resources than needed for most to just survive, living to the natural end isn't a challenge by itself. It is humanity as a species that is going. This is a time os despair, but also contemplation, as the last people just prepare to live their retirement.<br /> <br /> Now we have the question of the solution. A lot of interesting things can be used. Maybe the answer is in the PCs hands, and this is a Philosophical Epic about those heroes who can save humanity or fail in such a way that it won't even matter anymore, since there will be no one to care afterwards. Or the answer will be found by someone else and this is more of a personal chronicle about the PCs living throughout humanity's greatest hardship, similar to War of Worlds of H. G. Wells.<br /> <br /> Or maybe there are anwers that are so questionable that people have to choose between a heinous escape or letting humanity die out for the better. Like if the way to restore fertility is an Ordo riual that needs broken and tortured human slaves. This can make humanity live on to feed the vampires, but without anything but suffering for the living. Even if the answer isn't so awful, the people that find it and its nature will impact the future of the planet. This includes both the possibility of the God-Machine building a stopper in the process for some mysterious reason, or the possibility of the God-Machine not having complete control of the process. Maybe it is self-sabotage, or maybe supernaturals are, after all, beyond its grasp.<br /> <br /> Finaly, there's the outcome. An epilogue is likely a good end for such a game. If the world is doomed (by design or failure of the PCs), and no one will survive, think about what it is like for them to pass out. If supernatural creatures are tough enough, maybe the PCs, or some of them, live to see what is coming next. If the menace is stopped at any point, then the experience of the world with such disaster and the nature of the solution are going to shape the world forever, and any surviving PC should get the opportunity to watch this new world.<br /> <br /> You can find some inspirations in the 'last' books of the Classic World of Darkness, the Time of Judgement line. Also in some apocalyptic and post-apocalyptic stories, from Mad Max to the book I Am Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T08:40:01-07:00","id":989366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/988622-setting-idea-the-sterile-chronicle?p=988827#post988827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that sounds good. I could make it so that all living things are no longer reproducing, and fertile-based Magic is also failing for some reason. I'm planning that the God-Machine is causing this supernatural sterility, and has been slowly turning the fertility dial down since the 1940s, when the atomic bombs fell. Once all life has died off, it would create new life on the barren planet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think fertility magic should still work.<br /> <br /> It's just been moved to Life (Making), meaning that you must be a Master of Life, and thus Gnosis 5, Life 5 to create new life.<br /> <br /> You would also have your newly created life entirely vulnerable to being counterspelled by some random idiot unless you put a fuckton of effort into creating your new life, meaning that you wouldn't actually be able to stem the tide, only swim against it for a scant few moments.<br /> <br /> And of course, humanity's Symbol has become barren too, so these can't actually breed of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:07:12-07:00","id":989377,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the input, this will be very helpful, especially once I get the WOD books <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Would Discord be a good way to start up a game? It's the only thing I have on my phone, and I don't care much at all for Play by Post. It's too slow for me, and I'd like to get through a story in a few sessions, rather than a story a year, little by little a day, at the fastest pace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T11:06:58-07:00","id":990498,"title":"","content":"Mummys would be left with nothing but the sothic turn, right? Which would mean they'd awaken to Worlds devoid of humans, and/or possibly populated by new lifeforms. That's grim oO<br /> I guess the Ordo Dracul would get a huge amount of Slaves (the rank), looking to learn the coils of blood. With these, the ordo might even go on in its quest for Ascension long after humanity has died out. Still, that would be a smidgen of the former Vampire population.<br /> I'd expect Frantic attempts at increasing your lifespan to get &quot;more time!&quot; by various groups, e.g. Cheiron (what they would be willing to try to settle that Problem makes me shudder).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:20:13-07:00","id":990544,"title":"","content":"A really interesting thing to consider is that vampires would be fighting as hard as humans to save humanity. A parasite goes extinct if its host does. I was talking earlier about x-risk focused hunters, and how they'd be likely be Hunter standards to work with vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:42:39-07:00","id":990564,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this story is grim on one end, with humanity dying, but on the other end, it would be a new age of supernatural supremacy, finally able to live with fear of humanity's oppressive might smithing those who are caught, and threatening to end the supernaturals at any moment or mistake. It's a new age, built upon the ruins of a dead race. The Empire of Humanity has fallen into oblivion, now is the rise of the supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:56:15-07:00","id":990576,"title":"","content":"Well, vampires would go extinct without humanity, except maybe a small group of Dragons and a few who have supernatural patrons to feed them. Not sure Mages could keep going, either. As Manus mentioned, sterile humanity = humanity becoming metaphysically associated with sterility, meaning that mages would have to swim against the tide even more than they usually do to fight it. No humans quite possibly means no Arcadia and no Gentry, since Changeling heavily implies if not outright states that the Wyrd depends on humanity. It's kind of what differentiates it from the Umbra and Spirits- the Wyrd springs from narrative, which is a human concept. Prometheans...some of them might derive some pleasure from the world becoming as barren as they are. No humans would probably make becoming human massively harder, so they would have to pursue other avenues, even working with alchemists to try to use Pyros to save humanity. Mummies...wouldn't really like it, but in an apocalyptic scenario they'd be a natural fit to seize power. You might have a few Sin-Eaters making themselves deathlords of the wasteland, but most of them are connected enough to humanity that they'd take human extinction the way most humans would. Humanity going extinct means that the machine massively fucked up, because the books make it clear that for all its faults it is over all concerned with humanity surviving. It's possible that the sterility effect was the result of someone fucking it up, in fact. It would probably be frantically trying to revive humanity. A few Demons might consider a humanless world to be their Hell, but many more would probably want humanity back. Some Beasts might be onboard with the &quot;now the monsters are in charge&quot; thing, until they realize that no humans means it's massively hard for them to feed, and no human fears or human stories means that monsters have no place in the world. I'm not sure how you see the &quot;age of the supernatural&quot; happening when the supernatural is so dependent on humanity. You could say that the world becomes much more reliant on the supernatural, with much smaller human population that requires supernatural intervention to sustain it. <br /> <br /> The Pure would probably love it, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T10:41:35-07:00","id":991025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/988622-setting-idea-the-sterile-chronicle?p=990576#post990576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, vampires would go extinct without humanity, except maybe a small group of Dragons and a few who have supernatural patrons to feed them. Not sure Mages could keep going, either. As Manus mentioned, sterile humanity = humanity becoming metaphysically associated with sterility, meaning that mages would have to swim against the tide even more than they usually do to fight it. No humans quite possibly means no Arcadia and no Gentry, since Changeling heavily implies if not outright states that the Wyrd depends on humanity. It's kind of what differentiates it from the Umbra and Spirits- the Wyrd springs from narrative, which is a human concept. Prometheans...some of them might derive some pleasure from the world becoming as barren as they are. No humans would probably make becoming human massively harder, so they would have to pursue other avenues, even working with alchemists to try to use Pyros to save humanity. Mummies...wouldn't really like it, but in an apocalyptic scenario they'd be a natural fit to seize power. You might have a few Sin-Eaters making themselves deathlords of the wasteland, but most of them are connected enough to humanity that they'd take human extinction the way most humans would. Humanity going extinct means that the machine massively fucked up, because the books make it clear that for all its faults it is over all concerned with humanity surviving. It's possible that the sterility effect was the result of someone fucking it up, in fact. It would probably be frantically trying to revive humanity. A few Demons might consider a humanless world to be their Hell, but many more would probably want humanity back. Some Beasts might be onboard with the &quot;now the monsters are in charge&quot; thing, until they realize that no humans means it's massively hard for them to feed, and no human fears or human stories means that monsters have no place in the world. I'm not sure how you see the &quot;age of the supernatural&quot; happening when the supernatural is so dependent on humanity. You could say that the world becomes much more reliant on the supernatural, with much smaller human population that requires supernatural intervention to sustain it.<br /> <br /> The Pure would probably love it, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Vampires could continue to survive by entering torpor when their Blood Potency gets too high. By the end of it all, Prometheans would only have supernaturals and humans that used to be Prometheans to interact with. I'm sure they would find some way to reach the New Dawn and they would be considered an amazingly valuable resource by all supernaturals. I bet plenty of Prometheans would appreciate that their existence matters even if it would lead to horrific abuses. They would probably be encouraged to make a dozen or so other Prometheans in their lifetime to increase the population.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T10:44:58-07:00","id":991029,"title":"","content":"See, I'd still anticipate massive drops in the vampire population. Plus, no humans means no way to replenish it, meaning that any vampires that starve or die in other ways just bring it down more. Theoretically Prometheans could become human, but with no humans I think it would be phenomenally difficult, verging on impossible. Other Pilgrimages would probably be the most workable option. Argentum would probably become a very popular Refinement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:36:45-07:00","id":991124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/988622-setting-idea-the-sterile-chronicle?p=991029#post991029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I'd still anticipate massive drops in the vampire population. Plus, no humans means no way to replenish it, meaning that any vampires that starve or die in other ways just bring it down more. Theoretically Prometheans could become human, but with no humans I think it would be phenomenally difficult, verging on impossible. Other Pilgrimages would probably be the most workable option. Argentum would probably become a very popular Refinement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the population would certainly crash. Ghouls might be considered human enough for Prometheans presuming they still live in a human-like society. It would still be nightmarishly difficult though. In the end I could see the world population just being Prometheans (who are probably all Centimani by that point because the Pilgrimage would probably be impossible to complete) and Mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:40:30-07:00","id":991127,"title":"","content":"Amusingly, this might be something great enough to break the Pax Arcana over.<br /> <br /> The Ententes actually working together towards a single goal is a terrifying thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:19:48-07:00","id":991894,"title":"","content":"Funny thought: what if the sterility is so encompassing that you CANNOT get new humans AT ALL, not even through the Great Work? With the imago of humanity becoming barren and everything, to the degree even archmages are helpless, I'd feel taking this way out away would be fitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:37:18-07:00","id":991897,"title":"","content":"Then there is no point in playing at all.<br /> <br /> You just eliminated the entire point of Promethean, as well as the large parts of the points of Archmasters.<br /> <br /> We have a setting with a problem, the point of having this problem is probably to approach it from some angle with the hope of doing something, but if not even one of the most miraculous things in the setting can do anything, then it becomes a shitdark setting where there is no reason to do anything at all due to darkness-induced apathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:50:59-07:00","id":991962,"title":"","content":"I partially disagree. It isn't my favorite flavor of apocalypse, either, but It isn't pointless as a chronicle. So many stories can be told from an ultimately hopeless perspective. It does hurt the Pilgrimage, but a quest of hope doomed to fail, and the &quot;people&quot; doing that learning to cope with utter failure isn't a bad theme per se, much less a pointless one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:19:45-07:00","id":991981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/988622-setting-idea-the-sterile-chronicle?p=991894#post991894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">even archmages are helpless</div> </div> </div> </div>*Archmasters find symbol of their helplessness and kick it's ass on principle, and then fix the mess partially out of spite.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T08:09:05-07:00","id":992389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/988622-setting-idea-the-sterile-chronicle?p=991981#post991981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *Archmasters find symbol of their helplessness and kick it's ass on principle, and then fix the mess partially out of spite.*</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, that is always a possibility =P =D<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6042_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6042\" data-vbnamecard=\"6042\">ManusDomine</a> I know what you mean. You'd have to check with your players before pulling something like this. Still, I feel there are still themes worth exploring in a game like this, even as a Promethean/Archmage, as monteparnas said. Wouldn't be my cup of tea atm, either, but sometimes, something heavy like that would be interesting to play.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T09:17:47-07:00","id":992411,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile the God-Machine turns to the Demons all like &quot;See what happens when you fuck with my great works!?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}